('advanced-native-1548', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1548-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["她遇難仍繼續，並可用求助支援。"],"options":["句子重點是她被迫接收別人不想要的物品。","她遇難仍繼續，並可用求助支援。","她一遇不懂就完全放棄溫習。","她因繼續而拒絕任何幫助或方法調整。"]},"advanced-native-1548-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She tried to stick with it and asked for help.","She kept working on the topic rather than abandoning it.","She used support to carry on with the difficult parts.","She stayed with the task while changing how she approached it."],"options":["She tried to stick with it and asked for help.","She kept working on the topic rather than abandoning it.","She used support to carry on with the difficult parts.","She stayed with the task while changing how she approached it."]},"advanced-native-1548-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["I am trying to stick with the practice."],"options":["I am continuing only by refusing to review a method that is not working.","I am trying to stick with the practice.","I have given up the skill and stopped practising."]},"advanced-native-1548-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["要繼續就必須拒絕任何有用調整。"],"options":["要繼續就必須拒絕任何有用調整。","求助可以支持自己繼續練習。","困難時仍繼續投入。"]},"advanced-native-1548-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We can stick with the goal while changing a method that is not helping."],"options":["Use the repeated routine as the only measure of commitment, even if it blocks learning.","Treat asking for guidance as evidence that the person has abandoned the activity.","We can stick with the goal while changing a method that is not helping."]},"advanced-native-1548-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["We want to stick with the arts festival even though early bookings are low. We can improve the publicity and check what students want.","Sticking with the festival does not mean repeating unhelpful publicity. The team can explain the programme more clearly and review the response."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1549', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1549-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["熟悉節目帶來像老朋友般的安慰。"],"options":["節目因熟悉，就已證明是所有節目中品質最好。","Maya 完全不認得節目聲音，所以感到陌生。","熟悉節目帶來像老朋友般的安慰。","一位年長朋友搬進了 Maya 的新住所。"]},"advanced-native-1549-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The familiar voice makes the place feel less strange.","It brings a comforting part of my old routine into the new setting.","I enjoy having something I already know while I adjust.","It feels like an old friend in the new flat."],"options":["The familiar voice makes the place feel less strange.","It brings a comforting part of my old routine into the new setting.","I enjoy having something I already know while I adjust.","It feels like an old friend in the new flat."]},"advanced-native-1549-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The book feels like an old friend."],"options":["The reader has only just discovered the book and has no familiar memories of it.","The book feels like an old friend.","This describes an elderly character in the novel rather than the reader’s familiarity with the book."]},"advanced-native-1549-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["既然熟悉，它就客觀上優於所有新書。"],"options":["書本帶來熟悉與安慰。","既然熟悉，它就客觀上優於所有新書。","old 在比較中可以指長期熟悉，不是書本角色年老。"]},"advanced-native-1549-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Something can feel like an old friend while we still make room for new experiences."],"options":["Use familiarity as the only criterion before considering whether a new option suits the present need.","Put off exploring a suitable new place until the familiar object is no longer needed.","Something can feel like an old friend while we still make room for new experiences."]},"advanced-native-1549-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The familiar school piano feels like an old friend at this reunion. Many of us learned our first pieces on it.","Playing this school piano is like meeting an old friend. Its familiar sound brings back shared memories, even though newer instruments have their own s